    id: "3df34291f30bf6216b72",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "At least 4, including 3 children, killed in US elementary school shooting",
    summary: "Authorities have indicated that the shooter was killed by gunfire, though details remain scant about the attack.",
    preview: "Authorities have indicated that the shooter was killed by gunfire, though details remain scant about the attack. At least four people have been killed in a shooting at an elementary school in Oregon, part of the northwestern United States, according to statements from law enforcement. The shooting on Thursday took place at Silver Rail Elementary school in the city of Bend, about 160km (100 miles) southeast of Portland.",
    body: "Authorities have indicated that the shooter was killed by gunfire, though details remain scant about the attack.\n\nAt least four people have been killed in a shooting at an elementary school in Oregon, part of the northwestern United States, according to statements from law enforcement.\n\nThe shooting on Thursday took place at Silver Rail Elementary school in the city of Bend, about 160km (100 miles) southeast of Portland.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Two children killed when gunman fires into US Catholic school\n\n- list 2 of 3Children killed in mass shooting at Minneapolis Catholic school\n\n- list 3 of 3School shooting leaves multiple dead in US state of Georgia\n\nThree children were among the killed: They were ages 5, 8 and 11, according to Bend Police Chief Mike Krantz. A teacher was also reportedly among the dead.\n\nAuthorities have said the shooter was killed. Details about the suspect’s identity have yet to be released, but early reports indicate the attacker was 16 years old.\n\n“We’re in the process at this time of going room by room and evacuating each of the people who are in that school,” said Sheila Miller, the communications manager for the Bend Police Department on Thursday. “This is the kind of thing we never want to see happen in Bend. It’s devastating.”\n\nMiller said authorities received a call about a shot fired into a car outside the school at 12:59pm local time (19:59 GMT) and arrived on scene within minutes. Other emergency response calls were received during that time as well.\n\nThe number and condition of those injured were not immediately known. One child and a teacher were transported to a local hospital for treatment, Bend Police Chief Mike Krantz said in an afternoon news conference.\n\nKash Patel, the director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), said in a post on social media that the agency was on the scene assisting local law enforcement in the investigation.\n\n“We will make every resource they need available,” he wrote.\n\nOregon Governor Tina Kotek also said she was closely monitoring the situation.\n\nJeff Merkley, who represents Oregon in the US Senate, was among the political leaders to offer condolences in the wake of the shooting.\n\n“My heart is with the Bend community and all of the students and families affected. No one should have to fear violence at school,” he wrote in a post on the social media platform X.",
