    summary: "Ukraine's president has told Elon Musk that any restriction on the Starlink's system cost lives.",
    preview: "Ukraine says there has been a restriction to the speed of SpaceX's Starlink internet network in the country. Starlink - owned by Elon Musk - plays a vital part in the war between Ukraine and Russia, allowing Kyiv to guide drones to Russian targets and also protect itself. Elon Musk has suggested the US government may be behind the restriction on the speed at which some of Ukraine's weapons can travel and stay connect to the network. The BBC's Dan Johnson explores who has said what in the row and how the situation affects the war.",
    body: "Ukraine says there has been a restriction to the speed of SpaceX's Starlink internet network in the country.\n\nStarlink - owned by Elon Musk - plays a vital part in the war between Ukraine and Russia, allowing Kyiv to guide drones to Russian targets and also protect itself.\n\nElon Musk has suggested the US government may be behind the restriction on the speed at which some of Ukraine's weapons can travel and stay connect to the network.\n\nThe BBC's Dan Johnson explores who has said what in the row and how the situation affects the war.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- War in UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Volodymyr ZelenskyUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- RussiaUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Elon MuskUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- SpaceXUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- DronesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
